==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed UFO Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Manic Flying Cat''' when obtained from [[Forest Beasts (Deadly)|Bird Maniac]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Crazed Bird Cat can be good when stacked with proper meatshielding. They can be used to attack enemies like [[Shadow Boxer K]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Cow]] and [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion]], and other rather strong but short-ranged peons. Their disposability lets them be stacked easily and deliver high amounts of DPS in a small area. Compared to [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]], they have more survivability due to higher health (equivalent to Crazed Tank Cat at identical levels) and range. Unfortunately, their spawn cost is still quite high, lowering their usability in all forms.

They are also part of one of the only No-Gacha research Cat Combos, [[Aerial Recon (Combo)|Aerial Recon]]. However, this combo is useless if you have access to more efficient combos such as [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], or one of the Uber Rare research combos.

==='''True Form'''===
Manic Flying Cat gains more attack power and range in True Form. This makes Manic Flying Cat much more competent for DPS, as the increase in range is the most important out of the two, being the same as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. Unfortunately, due to the aforementioned cost of the unit, it is still situational in place of better [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|area attackers]] for the situation ([[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Courier Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] etc.).

Aside from the boosts in True Form, Manic Flying Cat is notably part of an efficient Unit Attack Up M combo, [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]], which can be put to great use on all other units you're bringing.

